{
  "id": "dungeon-game",
  "questionId": "dungeon-game",
  "slug": "dungeon-game",
  "title": "Dungeon Game",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "category": "Dp 2d",
  "patterns": [
    "dynamic programming",
    "grid"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "working forward from the top-left is tricky because the health requirement at a cell depends on the whole rest of the path ahead of it - what if you worked backward from the princess instead?",
    "define dp[i][j] as the minimum health the knight must have upon ENTERING cell (i, j) to survive from there to the princess",
    "at the destination cell, the knight needs enough health to survive that cell's value and still have at least 1 left: dp[m-1][n-1] = max(1, 1 - dungeon[m-1][n-1])",
    "for any other cell, the knight will move to whichever neighbor (right or down) requires less incoming health, then that path's requirement gets reduced by the current cell's value: dp[i][j] = max(1, min(dp[i+1][j], dp[i][j+1]) - dungeon[i][j])",
    "fill the table from the bottom-right corner backward to the top-left, and the answer is dp[0][0]"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "forgetting the max(1, ...) clamp, which is needed because health must always stay strictly positive, even on cells that heal a lot",
    "working forward from the start instead of backward from the destination, which doesn't correctly account for future health requirements",
    "off-by-one in health accounting - the knight needs health > 0 AFTER the cell's effect is applied, not just >= 0"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A knight needs to rescue a princess held in the bottom-right cell of a\n`dungeon` laid out as a grid. The knight starts in the top-left cell and\ncan only move right or down at each step. Each cell contains a number\nthat either adds to the knight's health (positive) or subtracts from it\n(negative or zero). The knight dies the instant its health drops to 0 or\nbelow, so it must have strictly positive health before entering every\ncell along its path, including the very first one.\n\n**Return the minimum initial health the knight needs to guarantee reaching the princess.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= rows, cols <= 200",
      "-1000 <= dungeon[i][j] <= 1000",
      "the knight can only move right or down",
      "health must stay strictly positive (> 0) before entering any cell"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "a single cell grid, whether positive, negative, or zero",
      "a grid where every cell is positive (minimum health is still at least 1)",
      "a path where health would dip very low in the middle even though the total sum is positive"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "dungeon = [[-2,-3,3],[-5,-10,1],[10,30,-5]]",
        "output": "7",
        "expectedOutput": "7",
        "explanation": "Starting with 7 health and taking the path right, down, down, right keeps health at 1 or above at every cell."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "dungeon = [[0]]",
        "output": "1",
        "expectedOutput": "1",
        "explanation": "The knight needs at least 1 health to be alive when entering the only cell."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "dungeon = [[100]]",
        "output": "1",
        "expectedOutput": "1",
        "explanation": "Even though the cell heals the knight, it still needs at least 1 health to begin with."
      }
    ],
